pwd (Print Working Directory) = to Check the current Directory
Terminal is an interface 
cd foldername => Change Directory
cd .. => go back to previous directory
ls => listing all the files and folder in current directory 
ls -la => detailed listing 
mkdir foldername => make directory 
example => mkdir test 
touch filename => to make a file
example => touch main.js
cat filename => To see data inside the file
example => cat main.js
vi or vim filename => to write something inside file
example => vim main.js 
After that press i for insertion mode 
To save the value 
press esc => then type :x or :wq! and enter to save the file 
mv => to move the file 
example => mv filename or foldername onwhich folder you have to move 
example => mv main.js JS 
It is also use to change the name
example => mv main.js index.js 
cp to copy the file   
cp index.js test 
cp -r folder1 folder2 
create a new file with samename and data
cp filename newfilename
cp index.js main.js 
rm -rf => to delete the file or folder
example => rm -rf main.js or rm -rf foldername 

node to open node compiler 
press ctrl+c to exit
